## How to trust these numbers

{{ confidence_header(posture) }}

{% if posture.report_through_date and posture.inv_ltm_net > 0 -%}
Every dollar in this report was pulled live from {{ org_display_name }}'s ERP invoice data on **{{ posture.report_through_date }}** (read-only). Topline figures are billed-not-collected and cover the trailing 12 months vs the same prior 12-month window — the only calendar-neutral comparison in a market-driven industry.
{%- else -%}
This report carries **no invoiced dollar figures**: {{ org_display_name }} has no ERP invoice data connected for this window. Every metric above is owned platform data — eCat orders and in-app activity — read live and current through today. That is the honest ceiling until invoice data arrives; see "What an invoiced ERP feed would unlock."
{%- endif %}

Two things worth your knowing:

- **One view of your business.** {% if posture.feed_completeness == "UNVERIFIED-SINGLE-FEED" -%}
  Invoice data is the single canonical source; cross-channel completeness cannot be claimed from one source alone. "Your invoiced business" is the honest framing, not "your total business."
{%- elif posture.feed_completeness == "PROVABLY-INCOMPLETE" -%}
  Confirmed eCat orders (${{ "{:,.0f}".format(posture.ecat_ltm_confirmed_gmv) }}) exceed invoiced LTM (${{ "{:,.0f}".format(posture.inv_ltm_net) }}) — the invoice number is provably a subset of your business. Every dollar here is capped at the partial confidence level.
{%- elif posture.feed_completeness == "STALE" -%}
  Invoice data last updated {{ posture.days_since_last_invoice }} days ago (> 45d threshold). Every dollar here is a snapshot of stale data; refresh before shipping.
{%- else -%}
  {{ posture.feed_completeness }} completeness state — see the notes below.
{%- endif %}

- **Rep identity is {% if posture.rep_identity_tier == 2 %}clean{% elif posture.rep_identity_tier == 1 %}partial{% else %}absent — behavior-only report, no rep-to-revenue{% endif %}.** {% if posture.rep_identity_tier == 2 -%}
  {{ posture.distinct_repnum }} of {{ posture.distinct_repnum }} invoice reps were named via the order-rep bridge ({{ posture.name_bridge_pct }}%). Every coaching card uses a named person, not a code.
{%- elif posture.rep_identity_tier == 1 -%}
  {{ (posture.distinct_repnum * (posture.name_bridge_pct or 0) / 100) | int }} of {{ posture.distinct_repnum }} invoice reps ({{ posture.name_bridge_pct }}%) bridge to names — below the 82% threshold, so the leaderboard and coaching cards render at rep-code grain without naming people.
{%- else -%}
  No rep-code-to-name bridge is available. Invoiced rep outcomes stay off; owned platform activity renders when Q-R1/R2/R4 are present.
{%- endif %}

**Directional figures are flagged where they appear.** Every other dollar in the report is a direct query result. Same data, same method, reproduces this report exactly.

